---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Gist from "../components/Gist.astro";
import gists from "../data/gists.json";
import SceneFurlans from "../components/SceneFurlans.astro";
import Rule from "../components/Rule.astro";
import Sources from "../components/Sources.astro";
import Plates from "../components/Plates.astro";
import Lightbox from "../components/Lightbox.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import Locator from "../components/Locator.astro";
import c from "../data/carnia.json";
const cmd = (x) => String(x ?? "")
  .replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g, "<strong>$1</strong>")
  .replace(/«(.+?)»/g, "<em>«$1»</em>")
  .replace(/(^|[^*])\*([^*\n]+?)\*/g, "$1<em>$2</em>");
const cmdp = (x) => cmd(x).replace(/\n\n+/g, "</p><p>");
---
<Base
  title="Back to Carnia"
  eyebrow="Mione · Paluzza · Ovaro"
  dek="Every account this family gives of itself begins in Carnia, and until now not one De Franceschi could be documented there. Here are twelve, across three villages — and the name is still at Mione in 1939.">


  <Gist g={gists.gists["carnia"]} />
  <section class="prose">
    <p>This is the archive's oldest open question. Carlo De Franceschi said the family came out of Carnia and settled in Istria <em>intorno al 1700</em>. A headmen's list of 1679 names a Zuane De Franceschi of Mione working in the imperial part of Istria with his son. Carlo added that in his own day, the 1870s, De Franceschi were still living at Mione and Muina.</p>
    <p>All of that is testimony. None of it was record. The Ovaro parish registers before 1806 are in no portal, and every sweep this archive ran through the Italian indexes came back with Tuscans, Venetians and Trentini and no Carnians at all.</p>
    <p>Searching by <em>place</em> instead of by name changed that.</p>
  </section>

  <Locator place="Mione di Ovaro" radius={14}
            note="Mione is a frazione of Ovaro, in the Val Degano — the Canale di Gorto of the 1679 headmen's list. Muina is the next hamlet down the valley." />

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);margin-top:34px">
    <div class="lab">Mione di Ovaro</div>
    <h3>The name is still in the village in 1939</h3>
    <p set:html={cmd(c.mione.found)}></p>
    <p set:html={cmd(c.mione.why)}></p>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">A bishop is a public figure and his dates are published; this archive names him for that reason and stops there. No claim of descent is made — what the record shows is that the surname persisted in the village the family's own tradition points to, for two hundred and sixty years after the only document that puts it there.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 style="font-size:30px;margin-top:50px">And then the registers of Mione itself</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">The Archivio di Stato di Udine has digitised the Napoleonic civil registers of the <strong>Comune di Mione</strong> — fifty-nine volumes — and publishes them openly. Nobody had looked.</p>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--terra);margin-top:24px">
    <div class="lab">The first three lines of the book</div>
    <h3>Defranceschi. Defranceschi. De Franceschi.</h3>
    <p set:html={cmd(c.mione.registers.index)}></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top:24px"><Plates ids={["mione-index"]} cols={1} /></div>

  <h3 style="font-size:24px;margin-top:38px">The households, as the acts give them</h3>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:16px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Where</th><th>Trade</th><th>The child</th><th class="m">Act</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{c.mione.registers.households.map(h => (
        <tr>
          <td>{h.who}</td><td>{h.where}</td><td><em>{h.trade}</em></td>
          <td>{h.child}<br /><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3)">{h.note}</span></td>
          <td class="m">{h.act}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top:24px"><Plates ids={["mione-1809-32","mione-1810-1","mione-1810-21"]} /></div>

  <h3 style="font-size:24px;margin-top:44px">{c.mione1806.heading}</h3>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.lead)}></p>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);margin-top:22px">
    <div class="lab">The act, as it stands on the page</div>
    <dl style="margin:10px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:6px 16px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6">
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">When</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.when)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">The parents</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.who)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">The child</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.child)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">Brought by</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.brought)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">Witnesses</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.witnesses)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">Signed</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.signed)}></dd>
      <dt class="lab" style="white-space:nowrap">Reference</dt><dd style="margin:0" set:html={cmd(c.mione1806.act.ref)}></dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">{c.mione1806.grade}</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
    {c.mione1806.why.map(x => (
      <div class="one" style={x.key ? "border-left-color:var(--accent)" : ""}>
        <div class="lab">{x.lab}</div>
        <div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px" set:html={cmdp(x.text)}></div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
    <p class="note" set:html={cmd(c.mione.registers.read)}></p>
    <p>The witnesses to these acts are worth reading too. A shoemaker and a tailor of Luint; a household servant; Lupieri Matteo, <em>possidente</em>. The registrar through all of them is <strong>Giacomo Micoli</strong> — the Micoli of Mione, whose family archive is listed on this archive's research log as holding the Gorto contracts that name the Erman who travelled to Istria with Zuane De Franceschi in 1679. The same dozen surnames run through the village for a hundred and thirty years.</p>
    <p><strong>What to do next is now obvious.</strong> The same series holds nine volumes of <em>Matrimoni</em> and thirteen of <em>Matrimoni, allegati</em> for Mione. In Napoleonic practice the <em>allegati</em> are the supporting papers filed with a marriage — birth extracts for the bride and groom, and often death extracts for their parents. A single De Franceschi marriage at Mione between 1806 and 1815 would therefore reach back into the middle of the eighteenth century, and possibly to the generation of the Zuane of 1679. Nothing else available to this project can do that.</p>
  </div>

